<title>HONG KONG: Min Xin interim net rises 54.83 percent.</title>
<headline>Min Xin interim net rises 54.83 percent.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1996-09-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months ended June 30</p>
<p>(in million HK$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (H.K. cents)	   14.75	vs 9.54</p>
<p>    Dividend (H.K. cents)    nil	  vs nil</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	  12.44 gain vs nil</p>
<p>    Net			    43.68	vs 28.21</p>
<p>    Turnover		     202.52     vs 54.79</p>
<p>    Company name		 Min Xin Holdings Ltd</p>
<p>    Books close		  N/A</p>
<p>    Dividend payable	   N/A</p>
<p>NOTE - Min Xin Holdings engages in investment holding, property investment, finance, banking and insurance.</p>
<p>Net is after an exceptional gain of HK$55 million on disposal of invetment property and loss of HK$42.55 million on provision for bad and doubtful debts.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6368</p>
</text>
